# build output
dist/
# throwaway builds: the ship loop tells agents to use `--outDir dist-$$`
# rather than the shared dist/, and those directories are disposable.
dist-*/
# agent working directory: harness scripts, generated data.csv/analysis.R, real R
# output and screenshots. Every run makes one and none has ever belonged in the
# repo — they run to tens of megabytes of regenerable artefacts. The harnesses
# worth keeping are described in docs/AGENT_BRIEF.md so the next run rebuilds them.
scratch/
# the regression battery, same species and same reasoning: a run builds one
# before its first commit, diffs its OUTPUT after each one, and describes what
# it asserted in docs/AGENT_BRIEF.md. It has never been tracked; the thirty-third
# run's reg/dump.mjs and the thirty-fourth's reg/dump-lib.mjs both stayed local.
reg/
# generated types
.astro/
# dependencies
node_modules/
# logs
npm-debug.log*
# environment variables
.env
.env.production
# macOS / Windows
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
HARPER.pdf
TRD and AP.pdf
